{
  "name": "AI Agent Session Manager with Timeout and Human Handoff",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3488822f-a12c-47fd-b3bb-bb224087e88d",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2144,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## AI Agent Session Manager with Timeout and Human Handoff\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow manages AI agent sessions from two webhook entry points: one for incoming user messages and one for control commands such as human handoff actions. It normalizes each request, loads shared configuration, routes the request to the correct branch, and uses data table records to evaluate, create, update, restore, or expire sessions. The control branch retrieves a target session, applies the requested state change, updates storage, and produces a control result.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the two webhook URLs for incoming messages and control requests in the systems that will call this workflow.\n- Set up the n8n Data Table used for session storage with fields required by the workflow, such as session ID, user/conversation identifiers, state, last activity time, timeout/expiry metadata, and handoff status.\n- Review the Load Configuration code node and set environment-specific values such as timeout duration, allowed commands, default session state, and table/field names.\n- Verify that the Normalize Input and Normalize Command nodes match the payload shapes sent by your messaging channel and control system.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the session timeout rules, command vocabulary, and session state transitions in the configuration and code nodes. You can also extend the control branch with additional human handoff commands or add downstream AI-response handling after Session Context."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e17cd638-2b22-4ddc-9574-1c6d41af3e64",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1584,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## Incoming message intake\n\nReceives standard user messages through a webhook and normalizes the payload into the common request format used by the rest of the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "47a446f8-16de-42bd-a5d2-3be9069a60e3",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1584,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Control command intake\n\nReceives administrative or human handoff control requests and normalizes them into the shared command format before routing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "33fe0c14-69b4-4c3a-b6cb-0c31a1f2e1a2",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1136,
        448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 352,
        "content": "## Shared request routing\n\nLoads workflow configuration for either request type and switches the flow between normal message session handling and control command handling."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d2797c95-c95c-48b4-8b69-8c392dd68758",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -688,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Evaluate message session\n\nLooks up the latest session for an incoming message, evaluates whether it is active, expired, missing, or needs restoration, and routes it to the appropriate session action."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c409f6e9-bced-4c3f-9eb8-617da9f4b214",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 688,
        "content": "## Persist session context\n\nUpdates session storage based on the evaluated state by expiring old records, inserting new sessions, updating activity, or restoring active sessions, then builds the final session context object."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5628d705-bf9c-40dc-8e77-b692bdca0cc3",
